PAPER.md.cuts: where every new line in PAPER.md and the README link comes from.

Everything else in PAPER.md is copied word for word: the head from README.md lines 1, 5-11 and 13-17,
each result from its folder files (named on each "_Source:" line, headings one level down, relative
links rewritten to repo-root paths, links to files never published in the repo kept as their plain
text), and the References from README.md's References section.
No sentence was composed freely. Approved sources are Ricardo's published repo text.

PAPER.md
- "# ai-biology: the full record"
  <- ai-physics PAPER.md:3 "# ai-physics: the full record" (repo name swapped).
- "This file puts the full record of every result in one place, for readers and reviewers who want
  it in a single document."
  <- ai-physics PAPER.md:21, verbatim.
- "Each section below is copied word for word from the result's own folder in this repository: the
  claim or bug report, the independent referee's verdict, and the prior-art check where there is one."
  <- ai-physics PAPER.md:21 ("the claim, the derivation or analysis, the independent referee's
     verdict, and the prior-art check"); "bug report" <- README.md:5 "bug reports";
     connectors "or", "where there is one".
- "The folders also hold the patches, repros and referee code."
  <- ai-physics PAPER.md:21 "The folders also hold the referee and certificate code."
     + README.md:47 "report, patches and repros".
- Challenges, VCC row: README.md:26, verbatim (rank as the repo states it: about 463 of 1,580).
- "Anthropic × Adaptyv Protein Design Competition: adaptyv-challenges. Submitted; lab results not out
  at the time of writing."
  <- README.md:25: name, repo link and Status cell, verbatim. Pointer only, no technical content.
- "Virtual Embryo Challenge: virtual-embryo-community. No challenge data or results are published here."
  <- README.md:27: name, repo link and its sentence "No challenge data or results are published
     here.", verbatim. Pointer only (Terms clause 14).
- Person headings "Manuel Irimia — ExOrthist and vast-tools", "Hugo Fernandes — pyglmnet",
  "Kris Sankaran — R packages", "Gavin Sherlock — GO::TermFinder",
  "Marcel Salathé — COVID-Twitter-BERT and lab repos"
  <- README.md:40, 49, 58, 65, 72, verbatim.
- "Manuel Irimia — M011, the ExOrthist membership score"
  <- README.md:46 "Separately, M011: the released ExOrthist membership score".
- "Victor Garcia — the NK-CTL model, VB10 / VB25 / VB31", "— the R script, line 35",
  "— codon-rate preprint, Fig 2B / Fig 2C", "— the Danish forecast"
  <- README.md:79 "Victor Garcia — the NK-CTL model and a codon-rate preprint", :83 "The model",
     :84 "line 35 of the released R script", :85 "Fig 2B", "Fig 2C", :86 "the Danish forecast";
     VB10/VB25/VB31 are the folder IDs.
- File labels ("Claim", "Verdict", "Prior Art", "Bugs", "Verdicts", "Referee", "Review",
  "Repositories", "Report", "PR 1: Bernoulli log-likelihood", ...) <- the file names, as in ai-physics.
- "# Contributions to AI-bio companies and open-source tools" <- README.md:94, verbatim.
- "Pull requests to AI-for-biology companies' public code, with their live status: README."
  <- README.md:96 "Pull requests to AI-for-biology companies' public code"; connectors
     "with their live status" (the README table is refreshed daily).

README.md
- "Every result in one file, with its claim or bug report, checks and verdict copied from the result
  folders: PAPER.md."
  <- ai-physics README.md:11 "Every result in one file, with its claim, derivation, checks and verdict
     copied from the result folders: [PAPER.md](PAPER.md)." ("derivation" -> "or bug report",
     from README.md:5 "bug reports"). Placed as in ai-physics: its own paragraph right after the
     retro link, before "Sister hubs".
